<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<!-- 
    WELCOME SCREEN (Welcome.fxml)
    
    This FXML file defines the user interface for the Welcome screen in the
    Eventra application. Think of it like a "front door" or "welcome mat"
    that greets users when they first open the application.
    
    WHAT THIS SCREEN DOES:
    - Displays the Eventra logo and brand identity
    - Provides a welcoming first impression for new users
    - Offers a simple button to enter the application
    - Creates a professional and inviting entry point
    - Sets the tone for the user experience
    
    KEY CONCEPTS TO UNDERSTAND:
    - First Impression: The initial screen users see when opening the app
    - Brand Presentation: Showing the Eventra logo and identity
    - User Onboarding: Guiding new users into the application
    - Simple Navigation: One clear action to proceed forward
    - Visual Design: Creating an attractive and professional appearance
    
    BUSINESS VALUE:
    - Creates a positive first impression for new users
    - Establishes brand recognition and professionalism
    - Provides a simple entry point that doesn't overwhelm users
    - Sets expectations for the quality of the application
    - Encourages users to explore the platform further
    
    REAL-WORLD ANALOGY:
    - Like a welcome mat at the entrance of a building
    - Like a reception desk that greets visitors
    - Like a front cover of a book that introduces the content
    - Like a lobby that welcomes guests to a hotel
    - Like a homepage that introduces a website
-->

<!-- 
    IMPORT STATEMENTS - JavaFX UI Components
    These statements tell JavaFX which UI components we want to use
    in our welcome screen. Think of them like importing tools from
    a toolbox that we'll use to build our interface.
    
    COMPONENTS EXPLAINED:
    - Button: Interactive button that users can click
    - ImageView: Container for displaying images (like the logo)
    - VBox: Vertical layout container that stacks elements top to bottom
-->
<?import javafx.scene.control.Button?>      <!-- Button component for user interaction -->
<?import javafx.scene.image.ImageView?>     <!-- Image component for displaying the logo -->
<?import javafx.scene.layout.VBox?>         <!-- Vertical layout container -->

<!-- 
    ROOT CONTAINER - Main Layout Structure
    This VBox is the main container that holds all the welcome screen
    elements. Think of it like the main frame of a picture that holds
    all the content.
    
    LAYOUT EXPLANATION:
    - VBox arranges all child elements vertically (top to bottom)
    - Think of it like stacking boxes on top of each other
    - All content flows from top to bottom in a clean, organized way
    
    PROPERTIES EXPLAINED:
    - xmlns: Standard XML namespace declaration for JavaFX
    - xmlns:fx: JavaFX-specific namespace for special attributes
    - fx:controller: Links this FXML to the WelcomeController Java class
    - alignment="CENTER": Centers all content horizontally on the screen
    - spacing="30": Adds 30 pixels of space between child elements
    - stylesheets: Links to the CSS file for visual styling
-->
<VBox xmlns="http://javafx.com/javafx"
      xmlns:fx="http://javafx.com/fxml"
      fx:controller="com.eventra.controller.WelcomeController"
      alignment="CENTER" spacing="30"
      stylesheets="@../css/styles.css">

    <!-- 
        LOGO IMAGE DISPLAY - Eventra Brand Identity
        This ImageView displays the Eventra logo at the top of the welcome screen.
        It's the first thing users see and establishes the brand identity.
        Think of it like a company sign that greets visitors.
        
        PROPERTIES EXPLAINED:
        - fx:id="logoView": Gives this element a name so the controller can reference it
        - fitWidth="300": Sets the logo width to 300 pixels (maintains proportions)
        - preserveRatio="true": Keeps the image proportions correct (no stretching)
        - pickOnBounds="true": Makes the entire image area clickable for interaction
        
        USER EXPERIENCE:
        - Users immediately see the Eventra brand
        - Logo size is appropriate for the screen
        - Image maintains its professional appearance
        - Logo can be made interactive if needed
        
        CONTROLLER CONNECTION:
        The WelcomeController can access this image using: @FXML private ImageView logoView;
        This allows the controller to:
        - Change the logo image dynamically
        - Make the logo clickable
        - Apply animations or effects
        - Handle logo-related interactions
    -->
    <ImageView fx:id="logoView"
               fitWidth="300"
               preserveRatio="true"
               pickOnBounds="true" />

    <!-- 
        WELCOME BUTTON - Entry Point to Application
        This button is what users click to proceed from the welcome screen
        into the main application. Think of it like a "Enter" button or
        "Get Started" button that welcomes users in.
        
        PROPERTIES EXPLAINED:
        - text="Welcome": The text displayed on the button
        - fx:id="welcomeBtn": Gives this button a name for the controller to access
        - onAction="#onWelcome": Calls the onWelcome() method in the controller when clicked
        
        STYLING EXPLAINED:
        - -fx-font-size: 16px: Sets button text size to 16 pixels for readability
        - -fx-background-color: #5C4DAA: Sets button background to Eventra brand purple
        - -fx-text-fill: white: Sets button text color to white for contrast
        - -fx-padding: 10 20: Adds 10px vertical and 20px horizontal padding for comfort
        - -fx-background-radius: 5: Makes button corners rounded (5px radius) for modern look
        
        USER EXPERIENCE:
        - Button is clearly visible and attractive
        - Text is easy to read with good contrast
        - Button size is comfortable for clicking
        - Rounded corners give a modern, professional appearance
        - Purple color matches the Eventra brand identity
        
        CONTROLLER CONNECTION:
        When clicked, this button calls the onWelcome() method in WelcomeController.
        That method handles what happens next, typically:
        - Navigating to the main menu or dashboard
        - Starting the user onboarding process
        - Transitioning to the next screen in the application
        - Initializing any necessary setup for the user session
    -->
    <Button text="Welcome"
            fx:id="welcomeBtn"
            onAction="#onWelcome"
            style="-fx-font-size: 16px; -fx-background-color: #5C4DAA; -fx-text-fill: white; -fx-padding: 10 20; -fx-background-radius: 5;" />
</VBox>

